>"weres" are properly call lycanthropes.

Actually, only werewolves are properly called "lycanthropes". (From
"lykos" ("wolf") + "nathropos" ("man"); it's Greek for "wolfman".)

The generic term would probably be "shapeshifter". (Note that the
"were" in "werewolf" is related to the Old English word "wer" (=
"man"), so "wererat" and "werejackal" are acceptable words.)

This has been a message from your neighborhood Etymology Queen...
